"""Warmage, Valda's Spire of Secrets 2024 (Mage Hand Press). Own wording."""
CLASS = {
 "eq": ["Leather Armor, Dagger, Staff (Arcane Focus), a Gaming Set of your choice, Explorer's Pack, 22 GP", "50 GP"],
 "f": {
  "Arcane Initiation": "Choose where you first learned the basics of magic. Each Initiation gives you two cantrips and a skill, as listed in its entry. You can also work with your GM to design your own. Pick one cantrip from any class list that suits combat and one that suits utility, avoid cantrips that belong to another caster alone, and pick one skill.",
  "Spellcasting": "You use the simple but potent magic of the Warmage. **Cantrips.** You know four Warmage cantrips and learn more as shown in the Cantrips column. Force Dart, Prestidigitation, Quickstep, and Shocking Grasp are good picks. When you gain a Warmage level, you can swap one cantrip for another Warmage cantrip. You cannot swap a cantrip that a Warmage trick needs unless you swap that trick at the same time. Cantrips granted by other Warmage features do not count against your total but are Warmage cantrips for you. **Spellcasting Ability.** Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for Warmage spells. **Spellcasting Focus.** An Arcane Focus works as a Spellcasting Focus for your Warmage spells. **Cantrip Spell Level.** For Dispel Magic, a Warmage cantrip counts as a spell whose level is half your Warmage level, to a maximum of 9.",
  "Warmage Edge": "Once per turn, when you cast a Warmage cantrip, you can improve it. **Intelligence to Damage.** Add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell if you do not already add it. **Improved Cantrip Upgrade.** From level 5, you also add extra dice to one damage roll of the spell, as shown in the Cantrip Bonus Dice column.",
  "Reliable Cantrip": "When a Warmage cantrip you cast at a creature misses on its attack roll, or the target succeeds on its save against it, the target takes the cantrip's minimum damage (if it deals any) and suffers no other effect. You can apply Warmage Edge to that damage, which is also minimum, but it cannot trigger Warmage tricks. Example: if Force Dart misses, you deal Force damage equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier.",
  "Warmage Tricks": "You learn special techniques that change how you fight, move, and cast. You know two tricks of your choice at level 2 and more at the levels in the Tricks column. Tricks are listed in the Warmage Trick Options. **Prerequisites.** You must meet a trick's prerequisite to learn it. A level prerequisite means Warmage level. **Replacing and Gaining Tricks.** When you gain a Warmage level, you can swap one trick for another you qualify for. You cannot take the same trick twice unless its text says so.",
  "Arcane Surge": "Once on each of your turns, when you deal damage with a Warmage cantrip, you can double its damage dice, as if it were a Critical Hit. If the cantrip already scored a Critical Hit, it deals triple the dice instead. You have two uses. A Short Rest returns one expended use. A Long Rest returns all of them. You gain a third use at level 11.",
  "Tactical Insight": "You add your Intelligence modifier (minimum +1) to saving throws against spells and other magical effects. This bonus does not apply to Intelligence saving throws.",
  "Arcane Surge Improvement": "You gain one additional use of Arcane Surge, for a total of three.",
  "Strategic Deflection": "When a creature casts a spell that forces you to make a saving throw to avoid damage, you can use a Reaction to redirect some of its energy. If you succeed on your save, pick another creature you can see within the spell's range or within 30 feet of you, whichever is closer. That creature, which can be the original caster, makes a saving throw against the spell using your spell save DC. On a failure, it suffers the spell's effects as if you had cast it and it had been the original target or in the area. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
  "Master Warmage": "When you roll Initiative and have no uses of Arcane Surge left, you regain one expended use."
 },
 "res": [{"n": "Arcane Surge", "tag": "Short Rest 1, Long Rest all", "reset": "long", "max": [0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]}],
 "lu": [{"feature": "Strategic Deflection", "n": "Strategic Deflection", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Reaction"}],
 "acts": {"Strategic Deflection": "reaction", "Arcane Surge": "free"},
 "opts": [{"feature": "Arcane Initiation", "title": "Arcane Initiation", "types": ["AInit"], "levels": [1]},
          {"feature": "Warmage Tricks", "title": "Warmage Trick", "types": ["T"], "col": "Tricks"}],
 "opt": {
  "AInit": {
   "Adventurer": "You learned magic informally by travelling with many mages. You learn the Mage Hand and Ray of Frost cantrips and gain proficiency in Perception.",
   "Arcane Event": "A surge of strange magic left its mark on you. You learn the Acid Splash and Message cantrips and gain proficiency in Insight.",
   "Circus Performer": "You picked up simple tricks for a sideshow or circus act. You learn the Minor Illusion and Starry Wisp cantrips and gain proficiency in Acrobatics.",
   "Mercenary": "You mastered the basics of war magic to fight other arcane soldiers. You learn the Mending and True Strike cantrips and gain proficiency in Athletics.",
   "Self-Taught": "You taught yourself the basics from an old tome or scroll. You learn the Fire Bolt and Light cantrips and gain proficiency in one skill of your choice.",
   "Survivalist": "You learned simple spells to survive in the wild. You learn the Druidcraft and Shillelagh cantrips and gain proficiency in Survival.",
   "Temple Initiate": "A temple or monastery taught you gentle healing magic. You learn the Sacred Flame and Spare the Dying cantrips and gain proficiency in Religion.",
   "Tower Apprentice": "You apprenticed under a spellcaster who taught you the basics of arcana. You learn the Prestidigitation and Shocking Grasp cantrips and gain proficiency in Arcana."
  },
  "T": {
   "Bishop's Maneuver": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Bishops. As a Bonus Action, you can expend a spell slot to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see. The distance is 15 feet times the slot's level.",
   "Blackjack": "Prerequisite: level 3, House of Cards, Darts, Dice, or Roulette. When you fail a D20 Test, you can roll another d20 and add it, which might turn the failure into a success. If the two d20s total more than 21, the test fails automatically. After you use this, you cannot use it again until you roll Initiative or finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Blasting Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when a Warmage cantrip deals Force damage to a creature, you can push it up to 10 feet straight away from you.",
   "Blinding Cantrip": "Prerequisite: Light cantrip. When you cast Light on an object you hold, you can also direct a flare at a creature you can see within 10 feet of you. It makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC. On a failure it has the Blinded condition until the start of your next turn. A creature that fails this save is immune to this effect for 1 minute.",
   "Capture": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Go. A formation you can use when you and three or more Allies without the Incapacitated condition are adjacent to an enemy on all sides, as if surrounding a cube. The enemy makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. On a failure, chains of force wrap it and it has the Stunned condition for 1 minute. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition and this formation on a success. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Castle": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Rooks. As a Bonus Action, choose a willing Small or Medium creature you can see within 120 feet. You and it teleport, swapping places. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Chips are Down": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Roulette. When you spend Chips of Fate on bets and lose at least one bet, you regain one expended Chip of Fate.",
   "Commander's Steed": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Kings. You can cast Find Steed once without a spell slot and regain this use after a Long Rest. When cast this way, the spell's slot level is your Warmage level divided by four, rounded up.",
   "Contingent Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. After a Long Rest, you can spend 10 minutes on a ritual to create a Contingent Cantrip. Cast a Warmage cantrip that takes an action or Bonus Action and deals no damage. It does not take effect now. It takes effect the next time you speak a chosen command word (no action needed). When you perform the ritual, choose whether it targets you, the nearest Ally, or the nearest enemy. You cannot apply Warmage tricks to it when it takes effect. You can have only one Contingent Cantrip. A new ritual ends the old one.",
   "Corrosive Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when a Warmage cantrip deals Acid damage to a creature, the acid erodes its defenses. The next attack roll made against that target before the start of your next turn treats its AC as lower by half your Warmage level, to a maximum of 5.",
   "Dartmaster": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Darts. When you cast a cantrip that makes several ranged spell attacks, such as Magic Daggers or Force Dart with Split Fire, and you miss with one or more, you can reroll all the misses and must use the new rolls. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Draining Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Whenever a Warmage cantrip deals Necrotic or Poison damage to an enemy, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half your Warmage level. They last 1 minute.",
   "Encryptogram": "Prerequisite: Cryptogram cantrip. When you cast Cryptogram, the message limit is 20 characters instead of 8. You can also encrypt it so only the chosen recipient can read it.",
   "Explosive Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when a Warmage cantrip deals Fire damage to a creature, you can cause a 5-foot Emanation explosion from the target. Each creature in it other than the target and you makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. A creature takes half the Fire damage rolled on a failure and none on a success.",
   "Extended Range": "Prerequisite: none. When you cast a Warmage cantrip with a range of 5 feet or more, you can double its range. You can also double the length of a Line, the size of a Cone or Cube, and the radius of a Cylinder, Emanation, or Sphere from your Warmage cantrips.",
   "Field Medic": "Prerequisite: none. You learn the Spare the Dying cantrip and can cast it as a Bonus Action. When you cast it on a creature with 0 Hit Points, the target regains 1 Hit Point and gains Temporary Hit Points equal to your Warmage level for 1 minute. A creature that regains Hit Points this way cannot do so again until it finishes a Long Rest.",
   "Flexible Range": "Prerequisite: none. Having an enemy within 5 feet does not give you Disadvantage on ranged attack rolls with Warmage cantrips. When you cast a Warmage cantrip that needs a melee spell attack, you can raise its range to 10 feet.",
   "Fold": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Cards. As a Reaction when an attack hits you, you can play your whole hand to cast Shield without a spell slot. Once you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Force Aegis": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 5, Force Buckler cantrip. You can concentrate on Force Buckler for up to 1 minute. It does not end early when an attack hits you.",
   "Force Breastplate": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Knights. While you have all your Hit Points, you have Resistance to all damage.",
   "Icy Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when a Warmage cantrip deals Cold damage to a creature, you numb it. The first time it makes an attack roll before the end of its next turn, subtract half your Warmage level from the roll.",
   "Infinite Variation": "Prerequisite: Prestidigitation cantrip. When you cast Prestidigitation, you can try to mimic another cantrip that deals no damage, even one not on the Warmage list. You must succeed on a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check or the spell fails. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for it, and it counts as a Warmage cantrip for you.",
   "Mage Hand Knack": "Prerequisite: Mage Hand cantrip. You can cast Mage Hand as a Bonus Action and control the hand as a Bonus Action each turn. When you control it, you can use one option. **Press.** The hand pushes a Large or smaller creature within 5 feet of it until the start of your next turn. Pick a direction away from the creature. Each foot of movement it makes in that direction costs 1 extra foot. **Punch.** The hand strikes a creature or object within 5 feet. Make a melee spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 Force damage. **Seize.** The hand tries to grapple a Small or smaller creature within 5 feet. The target makes a Strength or Dexterity save (its choice) against your spell save DC. On a failure it has the Grappled condition, with an escape DC equal to your spell save DC. The grapple lasts until the spell ends or you use a Bonus Action to control the hand.",
   "Magic Moment": "Prerequisite: Moment to Think cantrip. When you cast Moment to Think, you can also stop time for a creature you can see within 30 feet. It can take one action the spell allows during your turn, and you can interact with each other while time is stopped. You can take the Influence action, trade items, swap places with a willing creature within 5 feet, take the Help action for tasks during the stopped time, try to stabilize an Unconscious creature at 0 Hit Points, or hold a short private conversation.",
   "Minor Shadow Illusion": "Prerequisite: Minor Illusion cantrip. When you make the image of an object in an empty space with Minor Illusion, you can fill it with shadowstuff so it becomes partly real. It must still fit in a 5-foot Cube. It has AC 10 and 5 Hit Points, and weighs 5 pounds. You can have only one such object. While it exists, the cantrip requires Concentration. It cannot copy a creature, but if it shows an object that can deal damage, it can hurt creatures in its space. A creature that enters or starts its turn there makes an Intelligence save against your spell save DC. On a failure it takes 1d6 damage of a fitting type, which cannot trigger Warmage Edge or tricks. The damage rises to 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at level 11, and 4d6 at level 17.",
   "Mystical Armor": "Prerequisite: none. You can cast Mage Armor on yourself without a spell slot. While it is active, you add your Intelligence modifier to your AC instead of your Dexterity modifier.",
   "Mystical Athlete": "Prerequisite: Quickstep or Springheel cantrip. Quickstep raises your Speed by 20 feet instead of 10. Springheel raises your jump distance by 20 feet instead of 10. If you know both, you can cast both as part of the same Bonus Action.",
   "Mystical Retort": "Prerequisite: none. You learn the Vicious Mockery cantrip. When a creature you can see makes an attack roll against you, you can use a Reaction to cast Vicious Mockery at the attacker. If it fails its save, it has Disadvantage on that triggering attack roll instead of its next one, which may make the attack miss. After casting it this way, you cannot do so again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Mystical Vision": "Prerequisite: none. You can cast Detect Magic without expending a spell slot.",
   "Mystical Weaponmaster": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 5, Force Weapon and Magic Daggers cantrips. When you cast Force Weapon or Magic Daggers, you can use a Bonus Action to make one extra spell attack with that cantrip.",
   "Nudge Fate": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 5, Cheat cantrip. You can cast Cheat without Verbal or Somatic components. When you fail a D20 Test, you can nudge the d20 to one of the three sides next to the top face, which may turn it into a success. Or you can reroll the die and must use the new result. After you use this, you cannot use it again until you finish a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Opening Move": "Prerequisite: level 3, House of Bishops, Go, Kings, Knights, Pawns, or Rooks. In the first round of combat, the first spell attack you make has Advantage. You cannot use this if you have Disadvantage on your Initiative roll.",
   "Phantom Hookshot": "Prerequisite: Phantom Grapnel cantrip. You can cast Phantom Grapnel as a Bonus Action, but its range drops to 15 feet. When you cast it as an action, it pulls the target an extra 10 feet toward you.",
   "Prismatic Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when a Warmage cantrip deals Force damage, you can roll a d6 on the Prismatic Cantrip table to change the damage type for this casting. You can apply tricks as normal using the new type. You can also apply the trick that matches the rolled type, even if you do not know it. You can use this a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once) and regain all uses after a Long Rest. Table: 1 Acid (Corrosive Cantrip), 2 Cold (Icy Cantrip), 3 Fire (Explosive Cantrip), 4 Lightning (Static Cantrip), 5 Poison (Draining Cantrip), 6 Thunder (Silent Cantrip).",
   "Radiant Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, when you cast a Warmage cantrip that deals Acid, Cold, Fire, Force, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder damage, you can change its damage type to Radiant. When a Warmage cantrip deals Radiant damage, you can reroll one of its damage dice and must use the new roll. You can reroll 2 dice at level 11 and 3 dice at level 17.",
   "Rapid Fortification": "Prerequisite: Mending cantrip. You can cast Mending as an action or a Bonus Action. If you cast it as an action, you can use one effect. **Repair.** Restore one nonmagical object, such as a door, Cart, or window, to pristine shape if at least half its parts are present. It can be up to 10 cubic feet, or 1 cubic foot if very complex, like a clock. **Fortify.** Build a simple fortification up to 10 cubic feet, such as sealing a door, boarding a window, or raising a short stone wall. You need the materials on hand.",
   "Severe Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. When a creature rolls a 1 on the d20 for a save against one of your Warmage cantrips, it suffers a Critical Failure. It fails the save whatever its modifiers or your DC. If the spell deals damage, roll all its damage dice twice and add them, then add modifiers. The extra damage applies only to the creature that rolled a 1.",
   "Silent Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Once on each of your turns, right after a Warmage cantrip deals Thunder damage to an enemy, you can make a 5-foot Emanation of magical silence from the target, lasting until the start of your next turn. Creatures and objects fully inside have Immunity to Thunder damage, and creatures fully inside have the Deafened condition. Casting a spell with a Verbal component is impossible there.",
   "Snake Eyes": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, House of Dice. If you roll a 1 or 2 on a Die of Fate, you keep the die instead of giving it to the GM.",
   "Spellstrike": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 10, and the Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Frigid Blade, and True Strike cantrips. When you cast Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Frigid Blade, or True Strike, you can make two attacks as part of the spell instead of one. The cantrip's bonus damage applies to only one of them.",
   "Split Fire": "Prerequisite: Warmage level 5. When you cast a Warmage cantrip that needs one spell attack roll, you can pick several creatures and make a spell attack roll against each. You can target as many creatures as the cantrip has damage dice, and split the dice among them, with at least 1 die per target. Each attack must target a different creature. Example: Fire Bolt deals 3d10 at level 5. You can hit three creatures for 1d10 each, two creatures for 1d10 and 2d10, or one creature for 3d10.",
   "Static Cantrip": "Prerequisite: none. Whenever a Warmage cantrip deals Lightning damage to an enemy, you can store some energy as a charge that clings to you until the start of your next turn. While charged, when a creature you can see within 5 feet damages you, you can use a Reaction to deal Lightning damage to it equal to half your Warmage level."
  }
 },
}
